vaccines having  bought the highest number of vaccines  per capita  of any country in the world the pace of  that rollout is being criticized  by the opposition by some premiers and  by doctors and scientists who say  it's too slow with lives on the line  canada lags behind  several other countries in the number of  people being vaccinated  including the us uk and israel canada  has vaccinated fewer than 250  000 people while israel has vaccinated  more than 1.5 million  and the uk has vaccinated over a million  as well  there are reports that israel paid a  premium to get access to vaccines  faster i asked minister leblanc if  canada is willing to do the same  leblanc wouldn't disclose specifics but  said the cost  will be no obstacle we've said from the  beginning price  will not be a barrier for canada getting  as quickly as possible all of the doses  we need  so those companies know that it's not  some other country offering  some premium that's going to change the  delivery date to canada  we've said and we've successfully  negotiated with them  based on an extremely aggressive  procurement strategy  on friday federal officials said canada  will scale up its vaccine supply by the  end of february  but the provinces say they are running  out now with ontario premier doug  ford saying the province will run out of  vaccines within the next week  a claim minister leblanc disagreed with  if you knew you had  200 000 in a week how  sincere is it to say oh my god at the  end of the week we don't have any more  vaccines  of course you don't because there are  more coming next week and then the week  after there are even more  we'll have more on canada's slow vaccine  progress and what the government is  planning to do about it  sunday on the west block colleen  mercedes-stephenson in ottawa thanks  mercedes  a regimental funeral was held this  afternoon to honor a fallen calgary  police officer  the memorial for sergeant andrew harnett  was private but a procession took place  to allow  the public to pay tribute the 14-year  veteran of the force  died on new year's eve after being  struck by a vehicle during a traffic  stop  the 37 year old leaves behind his wife  chelsea who  is pregnant with their first child two  people are now facing first-degree  murder charges in connection with  harnett's death  just ahead the uk reaches a covet  tipping point  and the queen and prince philip received  their first vaccines  you're watching global national  the united kingdom has reached a new  grim pandemic milestone  more than 81 000 people have now died  from the virus  that's the highest death toll in europe  the uk  is also the first european country to  surpass 3 million  confirmed covet 19 cases the surge in  cases is  overwhelming hospitals right across the  uk many intensive care units are now  at or over capacity doctors are warning  the pressure on the health care system  is likely to worsen  in the coming weeks the country's  vaccine rollout has reached the royal  family  94 year old queen elizabeth has received  her first dose  along with her 99 year old husband  phillip a royal doctor administered the  shots at windsor castle  it's unclear which vaccine was given to  the couple whose ages put them in  britain's  second priority group royal sources say  the private matter was made public to  prevent speculation  india will begin the world's largest  vaccination drive in one week with the  goal of reaching  300 million people by july two  nationwide dry runs were done to prepare  for the mammoth rollout  the country has approved two covid19  vaccines  one by astrazeneca and oxford university  the other by  india's bahart biotech india's  population exceeds  1.3 billion with 10 million covet 19  cases  so far up next the electric car  revolution and the one country that's  leaving canada in its  dust  norway has become the first country in  the world where the majority of vehicles  sold are electric  in fact the nordic nation aims to  eliminate all gasoline car sales within  just  four years redmond shannon looks at how  canada compares and why  buying electric isn't always a simple  decision  norway peaceful progressive and  beautiful  a country that tends to find itself at  the top of all the good lists  so it's no surprise that norwegians now  buy more battery electric vehicles  than all other car types combined in  fact in 2020 only  17 of passenger vehicle sales were  gasoline or diesel  the most popular model in norway  in 2020 was the audi e-tron  and that is not a cheap car either in  in canada or in the uk or in norway  it's mostly down to big financial  incentives including an exemption from  import tax and the 25 sales tax  no annual road tax and large discounts  on tolls and ferries they can also use  bus lanes which is starting to become a  problem  a daughter of a friend of mine she said  to her father  look father there's a bus in the tesla  lane  it also helps that norway is rich its  wealth ironically coming from its  fossil fuel exports but in the end  that's what's going to have to happen on  an enormous scale  the money that was been made from fossil  fuels is going to have to be channeled  into  the clean technologies of the future  that we need one criticism of electric  cars  is the environmental impact of large  batteries  there needs to be a multi-pronged  strategy led by governments but also  participating by businesses  that mean that we can address the  sourcing issues  for the metals that are essential to go  into  battery electric vehicles in canada  where suvs and pickups dominate  electric vehicles make up less than  three percent of sales  those bigger vehicles have been a bit  slower coming on the electric side but  they're  they're they're coming quickly ottawa  offers a five thousand dollar incentive  quebec adds an eight thousand dollar  rebate  on top of that the trajectory is is  clearly there that's happening  the automakers are ramping up for that  you can see the sales trajectory is  going in that direction  gm says it wants to overtake tesla and  sell a million e-cars in north america  by  2025 but by then norway will have  eliminated  all gasoline vehicle sales canada's goal  is to do the same  by 2040 redmond shannon global news  london  and that is global national for this  saturday i'm colleen christie tonight's  your canada  is fireman's park in niagara falls  ontario  we love to see your part of our  beautiful country email your photos to  viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope you'll join us  again tomorrow have a great night  you
 

